# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. The model and the physics {#1-the-model-and-the-physics}"
msgstr "1. Model dan fisikanya {#1-the-model-and-the-physics}"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$H = -t \\sum_{\\langle ij\\rangle} \\left(b_i^\\dagger b_j + b_j^\\dagger b_i\\right), \\qquad (b_i^\\dagger)^2 = 0 .$$\n"
msgstr "$$H = -t \\sum_{\\langle ij\\rangle} \\left(b_i^\\dagger b_j + b_j^\\dagger b_i\\right), \\qquad (b_i^\\dagger)^2 = 0 .$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this model, bosons hop between neighboring sites $\\langle ij\\rangle$ of a square lattice. In principle, a site can hold any number of bosons; however,\n"
"**hard-core** bosons are forbidden to share a site. Thus, every site holds either zero or one boson. In `qiskit-bosons`, that is handled through the\n"
"truncation $d = 2$ (`max_occupation = 1`) during the boson-to-qubit mapping. Each site is then mapped as a two-level system and the model is the spin-1/2 XY model,\n"
"$b_i^\\dagger b_j + \\mathrm{h.c.} = \\tfrac12(X_iX_j + Y_iY_j)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam model ini, boson melompat antar site bertetangga $\\langle ij\\rangle$ pada kisi persegi. Pada prinsipnya, sebuah site bisa menampung boson dalam jumlah berapa pun; namun,\n"
"boson **hard-core** dilarang berbagi satu site. Jadi, setiap site berisi nol atau satu boson. Di `qiskit-bosons`, ini ditangani lewat\n"
"truncation $d = 2$ (`max_occupation = 1`) selama pemetaan boson-ke-qubit. Setiap site lalu dipetakan sebagai sistem dua-level dan modelnya adalah model XY spin-1/2,\n"
"$b_i^\\dagger b_j + \\mathrm{h.c.} = \\tfrac12(X_iX_j + Y_iY_j)$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**How this relates to the Bose-Hubbard model.** Bose-Hubbard adds an on-site repulsion $\\tfrac U2 n_i(n_i-1)$ to the hopping\n"
"term, which penalizes two bosons on one site. Hard-core is the limit $U \\to \\infty$, where double occupation is forbidden\n"
"outright. In the truncated space $n_i \\in \\{0, 1\\}$, $n_i(n_i-1) = 0$, so the on-site term vanishes whatever $U$ is\n"
"and the Hamiltonian has no interaction parameter at all. Note that this is the opposite of $U = 0$, which is the free\n"
"boson, where a site can hold many bosons.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Hubungannya dengan model Bose-Hubbard.** Bose-Hubbard menambahkan tolakan on-site $\\tfrac U2 n_i(n_i-1)$ pada suku\n"
"hopping, yang menghukum dua boson pada satu site. Hard-core adalah limit $U \\to \\infty$, di mana okupansi ganda dilarang\n"
"sepenuhnya. Dalam ruang terpotong $n_i \\in \\{0, 1\\}$, $n_i(n_i-1) = 0$, jadi suku on-site lenyap berapa pun $U$\n"
"dan Hamiltonian tidak punya parameter interaksi sama sekali. Perhatikan bahwa ini kebalikan dari $U = 0$, yaitu boson\n"
"bebas, di mana sebuah site bisa menampung banyak boson.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Why 1D is classically easy and 2D is not.** On an open chain, hard-core bosons are exactly free fermions: the Jordan-Wigner\n"
"transformation turns the spin chain into a quadratic fermion Hamiltonian with no string left over, because particles\n"
"cannot hop past each other. On a grid, a hop around a plaquette exchanges particles, and the sign that the fermions would pick up\n"
"is not matched by the bosons. The cells below check this with `qiskit-fermions`: they build free fermions that hop on the same\n"
"bonds, map them with `jordan_wigner` (qubit $j$ is mode $j$, sites numbered row by row) and compare the spectra with\n"
"the hard-core Hamiltonian in every particle-number sector. The hard-core matrix itself is built with plain numpy, because\n"
"it is a boson model.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Mengapa 1D mudah secara klasik dan 2D tidak.** Pada rantai terbuka, boson hard-core persis sama dengan fermion bebas: transformasi\n"
"Jordan-Wigner mengubah rantai spin menjadi Hamiltonian fermion kuadratik tanpa string yang tersisa, karena partikel\n"
"tidak bisa saling melompati. Pada grid, lompatan mengelilingi sebuah plaquette menukar partikel, dan tanda yang akan didapat fermion\n"
"tidak cocok dengan boson. Sel-sel di bawah memeriksanya dengan `qiskit-fermions`: mereka membangun fermion bebas yang melompat pada\n"
"bond yang sama, memetakannya dengan `jordan_wigner` (qubit $j$ adalah mode $j$, site bernomor baris demi baris) dan membandingkan spektrumnya dengan\n"
"Hamiltonian hard-core di setiap sektor jumlah partikel. Matriks hard-core sendiri dibangun dengan numpy biasa, karena\n"
"ini adalah model boson.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On the open chain, the two Hamiltonians are the same matrix and the spectra agree to rounding in every sector. On the grids,\n"
"they differ at order one, and the ring with an even particle number fails too, because particles can circle around it. So the\n"
"1D case is classically easy (free fermions are a polynomial problem) and the 2D case is the interesting one.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada rantai terbuka, kedua Hamiltonian adalah matriks yang sama dan spektrumnya cocok sampai galat pembulatan di setiap sektor. Pada grid,\n"
"keduanya berbeda pada orde satu, dan cincin dengan jumlah partikel genap juga gagal, karena partikel bisa mengitarinya. Jadi\n"
"kasus 1D mudah secara klasik (fermion bebas adalah masalah polinomial) dan kasus 2D adalah yang menarik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Build the `BosonicCircuit` {#2-build-the-bosoniccircuit}"
msgstr "2. Bangun `BosonicCircuit` {#2-build-the-bosoniccircuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A hopping term is Hermitian only together with its conjugate pair, so both stay in one group. Bonds that share no site commute, so an\n"
"**edge coloring** of the square lattice gives groups that commute internally at the bosonic level:\n"
msgstr ""
"Suku hopping hanya Hermitian bersama pasangan konjugatnya, jadi keduanya tetap dalam satu grup. Bond yang tidak berbagi site saling komut, sehingga\n"
"**edge coloring** kisi persegi memberi grup yang komut secara internal di level bosonik:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "color 0 / 1: horizontal bonds starting at an even / odd column (blue pair)\n"
msgstr "warna 0 / 1: bond horizontal yang dimulai di kolom genap / ganjil (pasangan biru)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "color 2 / 3: vertical bonds starting at an even / odd row (orange and red)\n"
msgstr "warna 2 / 3: bond vertikal yang dimulai di baris genap / ganjil (oranye dan merah)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Two bonds of the same color never share a site, because the bonds along a line alternate colors. The construction below takes\n"
"only the lattice size $(L_x, L_y)$ as input, and everything after it (circuit, encoding, transpilation) is identical for every\n"
"size. The drawing shows the site numbering ($s = L_x y + x$) and the colors for a $4\\times4$ lattice.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dua bond dengan warna sama tidak pernah berbagi site, karena bond sepanjang satu garis berganti warna. Konstruksi di bawah hanya\n"
"mengambil ukuran kisi $(L_x, L_y)$ sebagai input, dan semua yang sesudahnya (circuit, encoding, transpilasi) identik untuk setiap\n"
"ukuran. Gambar menunjukkan penomoran site ($s = L_x y + x$) dan warna untuk kisi $4\\times4$.\n"

