# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Compute a Néel quench {#3-compute-a-néel-quench}"
msgstr "3. Hitung Néel quench {#3-compute-a-néel-quench}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can now watch the bosons move under a quench. The dynamics start from a **Néel pattern**: the sites of a checkerboard are alternately\n"
"filled with one boson (black circles in the drawing below) and empty (white circles), so half of the sites are occupied. At\n"
"time zero, the state is a single bit string, which is easy to prepare (one `X` gate per occupied site). It is not an eigenstate of\n"
"the hopping Hamiltonian: every bond of the lattice joins an occupied and an empty site, so every bond can move a boson,\n"
"and the state starts to change right away. Preparing a simple state and then letting it evolve under a Hamiltonian that it\n"
"is not an eigenstate of is called a **quench**.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang kamu bisa melihat boson bergerak di bawah quench. Dinamikanya dimulai dari **pola Néel**: site pada papan catur diisi bergantian\n"
"dengan satu boson (lingkaran hitam di gambar di bawah) dan kosong (lingkaran putih), jadi separuh site terisi. Pada\n"
"waktu nol, state-nya adalah satu bit string, yang mudah disiapkan (satu gate `X` per site terisi). State ini bukan eigenstate dari\n"
"Hamiltonian hopping: setiap bond pada kisi menghubungkan site terisi dan site kosong, jadi setiap bond bisa memindahkan boson,\n"
"dan state mulai berubah seketika. Menyiapkan state sederhana lalu membiarkannya berevolusi di bawah Hamiltonian yang bukan\n"
"eigenstate-nya disebut **quench**.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/hard-core-bosons-dynamics/extracted-outputs/d8ccb302-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/hard-core-bosons-dynamics/extracted-outputs/d8ccb302-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because the lattice is bipartite, a hop always moves a boson to the other sublattice of the checkerboard. This suggests the\n"
"observable to follow, the **staggered density imbalance**\n"
msgstr ""
"Karena kisinya bipartit, sebuah lompatan selalu memindahkan boson ke sublattice lain pada papan catur. Ini mengisyaratkan\n"
"observable yang diikuti, yaitu **ketidakseimbangan densitas staggered**\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$\\mathcal I(t) = \\frac1N \\sum_i (-1)^{x_i+y_i}\\,\\bigl(2\\langle n_i\\rangle(t) - 1\\bigr) = \\frac{2}{N}\\bigl(N_A(t) - N_B(t)\\bigr),$$\n"
msgstr "$$\\mathcal I(t) = \\frac1N \\sum_i (-1)^{x_i+y_i}\\,\\bigl(2\\langle n_i\\rangle(t) - 1\\bigr) = \\frac{2}{N}\\bigl(N_A(t) - N_B(t)\\bigr),$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $N_A$ and $N_B$ are the numbers of bosons on the two sublattices. It measures how many bosons are still on the\n"
"sublattice they started on. It starts at $\\mathcal I = 1$ and, as the bosons spread over the lattice, falls and then\n"
"fluctuates around zero, where neither sublattice is preferred. On hardware, it is cheap to measure, because it only needs\n"
"the occupation of each site, that is, single-qubit $Z$ measurements.\n"
msgstr ""
"dengan $N_A$ dan $N_B$ adalah jumlah boson pada kedua sublattice. Ia mengukur berapa banyak boson yang masih berada di\n"
"sublattice tempat mereka mulai. Nilainya dimulai dari $\\mathcal I = 1$ dan, saat boson menyebar di kisi, turun lalu\n"
"berfluktuasi di sekitar nol, di mana tidak ada sublattice yang lebih disukai. Di hardware, ini murah diukur, karena hanya membutuhkan\n"
"okupansi tiap site, yaitu pengukuran $Z$ satu-qubit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The later plots of the observable behavior also show the density of individual sites.\n"
"In one dimension, this quench is a free-fermion problem, but on a square lattice it is not (as discussed in section 1), so the exact evolution of the $4\\times4$ lattice below is the reference. The hard-core Hilbert space is the set of bit strings, and $b_i^\\dagger b_j$ moves a bit. Build $H$ as a sparse matrix with plain numpy and evolve with `expm_multiply`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Plot perilaku observable selanjutnya juga menampilkan densitas tiap site.\n"
"Dalam satu dimensi, quench ini adalah masalah fermion bebas, tetapi pada kisi persegi tidak (seperti dibahas di bagian 1), jadi evolusi eksak kisi $4\\times4$ di bawah adalah referensinya. Ruang Hilbert hard-core adalah himpunan bit string, dan $b_i^\\dagger b_j$ memindahkan satu bit. Bangun $H$ sebagai matriks sparse dengan numpy biasa dan evolusikan dengan `expm_multiply`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, compute the exact reference.\n"
msgstr "Pertama, hitung referensi eksaknya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, check the `InitializeModes` gate, which also confirms that the mode-to-qubit encoding is correct.\n"
msgstr "Selanjutnya, periksa gate `InitializeModes`, yang juga mengonfirmasi bahwa encoding mode-ke-qubit sudah benar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now compute the Trotterized curves. A circuit is one first-order Trotter step of length $dt$ (all four colors once), applied\n"
"$T/dt$ times; `trotter_series` returns the site densities at every multiple of $dt$. The cell after it turns the densities of\n"
"the exact and of the Trotterized evolution into the three observables to plot.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang hitung kurva Trotterized. Sebuah circuit adalah satu langkah Trotter orde pertama dengan panjang $dt$ (keempat warna sekali), diterapkan\n"
"$T/dt$ kali; `trotter_series` mengembalikan densitas site pada setiap kelipatan $dt$. Sel sesudahnya mengubah densitas dari\n"
"evolusi eksak dan evolusi Trotterized menjadi tiga observable untuk diplot.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/hard-core-bosons-dynamics/extracted-outputs/dd335add-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/hard-core-bosons-dynamics/extracted-outputs/dd335add-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here $dt = T/\\text{steps}$ is the length of one Trotter step, so the legend gives both. All three panels show all three step\n"
"sizes. The smaller the step, the closer the circuit follows the exact curve. The coarsest step, $dt = 0.5$, visibly misses it in places, and even $dt = 0.1$ shows a small wobble on the corner site near $t \\approx 1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sini $dt = T/\\text{steps}$ adalah panjang satu langkah Trotter, jadi legenda memberikan keduanya. Ketiga panel menampilkan ketiga ukuran\n"
"langkah. Semakin kecil langkahnya, semakin dekat circuit mengikuti kurva eksak. Langkah paling kasar, $dt = 0.5$, terlihat meleset di beberapa tempat, dan bahkan $dt = 0.1$ menunjukkan sedikit goyangan pada site sudut di sekitar $t \\approx 1$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Quantify the Trotter error {#4-quantify-the-trotter-error}"
msgstr "4. Kuantifikasi error Trotter {#4-quantify-the-trotter-error}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The only numerical error of the circuit is the **Trotter error between the colors** at the bosonic level. The other two\n"
"places where an error could creep in are exact by construction:\n"
msgstr ""
"Satu-satunya error numerik pada circuit adalah **error Trotter antar warna** di level bosonik. Dua tempat lain\n"
"tempat error bisa menyelinap eksak secara konstruksi:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The qubit side.** The Pauli terms of one color commute, because the bonds of a color share no site. Synthesizing a color\n"
"therefore needs no further approximation, and the circuit is the ordered product of the exact color exponentials.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Sisi qubit.** Suku Pauli dalam satu warna saling komut, karena bond dalam satu warna tidak berbagi site. Mensintesis satu warna\n"
"jadi tidak memerlukan hampiran tambahan, dan circuit adalah hasil kali berurutan dari eksponensial warna yang eksak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The encoding.** At $d = 2$, the four `LevelEncoding`s are different representations of the same two-level system, so they\n"
"give the same circuit up to cost (section 5).\n"
msgstr ""
"**Encoding-nya.** Pada $d = 2$, keempat `LevelEncoding` adalah representasi berbeda dari sistem dua level yang sama, jadi\n"
"menghasilkan circuit yang sama sampai ke biayanya (bagian 5).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There is no \"truncation\" error either: the cutoff $d = 2$ *defines* this model (section 1). It is not a numerical\n"
"approximation of something larger.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tidak ada error \"pemotongan\" (truncation) juga: cutoff $d = 2$ *mendefinisikan* model ini (bagian 1). Ini bukan\n"
"pendekatan numerik dari sesuatu yang lebih besar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This section explores `BosonicSuzukiTrotter`. It measures the Trotter error against the exact reference of section 3 at one final time, $T = 2$, versus\n"
"the number of steps, for first and for second order. It uses $T = 2$, not the end of the curves above, on purpose: by\n"
"$t = 3$, the signal has decayed close to its long-time value, so the error there is small and scatters from one step count to\n"
"the next. At $T = 2$, the dynamics are still pronounced.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bagian ini menjelajahi `BosonicSuzukiTrotter`. Bagian ini mengukur error Trotter terhadap referensi eksak dari bagian 3 pada satu waktu akhir, $T = 2$, terhadap\n"
"jumlah langkah, untuk orde pertama dan kedua. Kita memakai $T = 2$, bukan ujung kurva di atas, dengan sengaja: pada\n"
"$t = 3$, sinyal sudah meluruh mendekati nilai jangka panjangnya, jadi errornya kecil dan menyebar dari satu jumlah langkah\n"
"ke jumlah langkah berikutnya. Pada $T = 2$, dinamikanya masih jelas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Is the bosonic level needed for this error?** For hard-core bosons, the qubit operator is only $-\\tfrac12(XX + YY)$ per bond,\n"
"so you can also hand it to Qiskit as **one** `PauliEvolutionGate`, without any groups, and let Qiskit's `SuzukiTrotter` product formula split it. A product formula applies the terms in the order it is\n"
"given, so the order decides which terms are exponentiated together. Try three: the terms sorted by edge color (the grouping\n"
"that the bosonic circuit knows), the terms bond by bond, and `preserve_order=False`, which lets Qiskit reorder the terms\n"
"itself.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Apakah level bosonik diperlukan untuk error ini?** Untuk boson hard-core, operator qubit-nya hanya $-\\tfrac12(XX + YY)$ per ikatan,\n"
"jadi kamu juga bisa menyerahkannya ke Qiskit sebagai **satu** `PauliEvolutionGate`, tanpa grup apa pun, dan membiarkan `SuzukiTrotter` milik Qiskit memecahnya dengan product formula. Product formula menerapkan suku-suku sesuai urutan yang\n"
"diberikan, jadi urutan menentukan suku mana yang dieksponensialkan bersama. Coba tiga cara: suku diurutkan menurut warna sisi (pengelompokan\n"
"yang dikenal circuit bosonik), suku ikatan demi ikatan, dan `preserve_order=False`, yang membiarkan Qiskit mengurutkan ulang suku-suku\n"
"sendiri.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/hard-core-bosons-dynamics/extracted-outputs/11884bb1-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/hard-core-bosons-dynamics/extracted-outputs/11884bb1-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Left:** the dotted gray lines are the ideal slopes $-1$ and $-2$, and the fitted slope over the last three points of each\n"
"curve is in the legend. The slopes approach the ideal values only once the step is small enough; with few steps, the error is\n"
"outside the asymptotic regime.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kiri:** garis abu-abu putus-putus adalah kemiringan ideal $-1$ dan $-2$, dan kemiringan hasil fit pada tiga titik terakhir tiap\n"
"kurva ada di legenda. Kemiringannya baru mendekati nilai ideal setelah langkahnya cukup kecil; dengan sedikit langkah, error\n"
"berada di luar rezim asimtotik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Right:** the same errors against the two-qubit depth of the whole circuit, for the same step\n"
"counts. A second-order step has more blocks (14 against 8 layers for one step), but adjacent identical blocks of neighboring\n"
"repetitions merge. For large errors (one or two steps), first order is the cheaper way to reach a given error. Below an error of about $10^{-1}$, second order is cheaper.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kanan:** error yang sama terhadap kedalaman dua-qubit dari seluruh circuit, untuk jumlah langkah yang sama. Satu langkah orde kedua punya lebih banyak\n"
"blok (14 lawan 8 layer untuk satu langkah), tetapi blok identik yang bersebelahan dari pengulangan yang berdekatan bergabung. Untuk error besar (satu atau dua langkah), orde pertama adalah cara yang lebih murah untuk mencapai error tertentu. Di bawah error sekitar $10^{-1}$, orde kedua lebih murah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Single gates.** The dashed curves are the single `PauliEvolutionGate` with `SuzukiTrotter` of order 1 (green) and 2 (blue). Each\n"
"ordering of the Pauli terms has its own marker and a lighter tint of the color. With the terms sorted by color (crosses), the\n"
"single gate lies exactly on the bosonic curve of the same order: it is the same product formula. In the other two orderings,\n"
"it is a different formula with a different error, which can be several times larger or (at one or two steps) smaller. But the\n"
"**order of magnitude and the scaling match** the bosonic circuit: the first-order curves fall with the ideal slope $-1$ and the\n"
"second-order curves with $-2$, and at 32 steps all three orderings are within a factor of about three of each other. So the Trotter\n"
"error does not decide between the approaches. What differs is the cost (right panel, and the next section): at equal error,\n"
"the squares (medium tint) need a much larger depth, and the triangles (lightest tint) roughly twice the depth of the crosses. At the bosonic level, the\n"
"grouping is part of the operator, so there is no ordering to choose by hand, which makes for a much more ergonomic workflow.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Gate tunggal.** Kurva putus-putus adalah `PauliEvolutionGate` tunggal dengan `SuzukiTrotter` orde 1 (hijau) dan 2 (biru). Setiap\n"
"urutan suku Pauli punya penanda sendiri dan warna yang lebih terang. Dengan suku diurutkan menurut warna (tanda silang),\n"
"gate tunggal itu tepat berada di atas kurva bosonik dengan orde yang sama: ini product formula yang sama. Pada dua urutan lainnya,\n"
"formulanya berbeda dengan error yang berbeda, yang bisa beberapa kali lebih besar atau (pada satu atau dua langkah) lebih kecil. Tetapi\n"
"**orde besaran dan skalanya cocok** dengan circuit bosonik: kurva orde pertama turun dengan kemiringan ideal $-1$ dan kurva\n"
"orde kedua dengan $-2$, dan pada 32 langkah ketiga urutan berada dalam faktor sekitar tiga satu sama lain. Jadi error\n"
"Trotter tidak menentukan pilihan antar pendekatan. Yang berbeda adalah biayanya (panel kanan, dan bagian berikutnya): pada error yang sama,\n"
"persegi (warna sedang) butuh kedalaman jauh lebih besar, dan segitiga (warna paling terang) sekitar dua kali kedalaman tanda silang. Pada level bosonik,\n"
"pengelompokan adalah bagian dari operator, jadi tidak ada urutan yang perlu dipilih manual, sehingga alur kerjanya jauh lebih ergonomis.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "5. Scale with system size {#5-scale-with-system-size}"
msgstr "5. Skala terhadap ukuran sistem {#5-scale-with-system-size}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This section investigates how cost scales with the lattice size. Since one Trotter step is one $XX+YY$ layer per color, whatever the\n"
"number of sites, the two-qubit **depth should be flat** in the lattice size while the **gate count grows** with the number of\n"
"bonds. The sizes go up to $10\\times12$, the whole Nighthawk chip in the compact codes. The unary codes need two qubits\n"
"per mode, so they stop at the sizes that fit in 120 qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bagian ini menyelidiki bagaimana biaya berskala terhadap ukuran lattice. Karena satu langkah Trotter adalah satu layer $XX+YY$ per warna, berapa pun\n"
"jumlah situs, **kedalaman** dua-qubit **seharusnya datar** terhadap ukuran lattice sementara **jumlah gate bertambah** sesuai jumlah\n"
"ikatan. Ukurannya naik sampai $10\\times12$, seluruh chip Nighthawk dalam kode kompak. Kode unary butuh dua qubit\n"
"per mode, jadi berhenti pada ukuran yang muat dalam 120 qubit.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/hard-core-bosons-dynamics/extracted-outputs/d4dbf1ea-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/hard-core-bosons-dynamics/extracted-outputs/d4dbf1ea-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The compact code has a flat depth from $3\\times3$ on (every color is a layer of side-by-side $XX+YY$ rotations; the $2\\times2$\n"
"lattice has only two colors, so its depth is half) and a gate count that grows with the number of bonds.\n"
"The unary codes are an order of magnitude more expensive in both. The reason is simple: in the compact codes, a bond maps to one $XX$ and\n"
"one $YY$ term on the two qubits of the bond with equal coefficients, that is, an $XX+YY$ rotation (two `cz`). In the unary codes, each\n"
"mode has two qubits (one per level), and the hop expands into several weight-4 Pauli strings on the four qubits of both\n"
"modes. They all commute, so nothing is saved by commutation. The ratio is a property of the encoding at $d = 2$, and it does\n"
"not change with the lattice size. At $d = 2$, the standard-binary and Gray codes are the same code, and the projected and\n"
"unprojected unary codes emit the same operator, so the compact curve stands for both pairs.\n"
"**Why Trotterize at the bosonic level?** The dashed curves are the same Trotter steps as one `PauliEvolutionGate` over the qubit\n"
"operator (section 4), in green for first order and blue for second order. The solid blue curve is the second-order bosonic circuit,\n"
"the solid green curve the first-order one from above. The single gate with the terms sorted by color (crosses) lies exactly on the\n"
"bosonic curve of its order: a flat depth (8 for first order, 14 for second order) and the minimal gate count (as in the previous section). Qiskit does not find\n"
"that grouping by itself. If the terms are listed bond by bond (squares), the gate count is the same, but the layers are not packed\n"
"and the depth grows with the lattice (at $10\\times12$ it is 84 against 8 for first order and 166 against 14 for second order).\n"
"With `preserve_order=False` (triangles), Qiskit does find commuting terms and the depth stays flat, but it treats the XX and the YY\n"
"term of a bond as separate rotations, so it needs about a third more two-qubit gates and twice the depth. So the bosonic level is\n"
"not magic: it carries the edge coloring in the operator itself, and what you would otherwise have to arrange by hand in the Pauli\n"
"terms (and keep arranged for every lattice) comes with the construction.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kode kompak punya kedalaman datar mulai dari $3\\times3$ (setiap warna adalah satu layer rotasi $XX+YY$ yang berdampingan; lattice $2\\times2$\n"
"hanya punya dua warna, jadi kedalamannya setengah) dan jumlah gate yang bertambah sesuai jumlah ikatan.\n"
"Kode unary lebih mahal satu orde besaran pada keduanya. Alasannya sederhana: pada kode kompak, satu ikatan dipetakan ke satu suku $XX$ dan\n"
"satu suku $YY$ pada dua qubit dari ikatan itu dengan koefisien yang sama, yaitu rotasi $XX+YY$ (dua `cz`). Pada kode unary, setiap\n"
"mode punya dua qubit (satu per level), dan hop-nya berkembang menjadi beberapa string Pauli berbobot 4 pada keempat qubit dari kedua\n"
"mode. Semuanya komut, jadi komutasi tidak menghemat apa-apa. Rasionya adalah sifat dari encoding pada $d = 2$, dan\n"
"tidak berubah terhadap ukuran lattice. Pada $d = 2$, kode standard-binary dan Gray adalah kode yang sama, dan kode unary terproyeksi dan\n"
"tak terproyeksi menghasilkan operator yang sama, jadi kurva kompak mewakili kedua pasangan.\n"
"**Kenapa Trotterize di level bosonik?** Kurva putus-putus adalah langkah Trotter yang sama sebagai satu `PauliEvolutionGate` atas operator\n"
"qubit (bagian 4), hijau untuk orde pertama dan biru untuk orde kedua. Kurva biru solid adalah circuit bosonik orde kedua,\n"
"kurva hijau solid adalah yang orde pertama dari atas. Gate tunggal dengan suku diurutkan menurut warna (tanda silang) tepat berada di atas\n"
"kurva bosonik dengan ordenya: kedalaman datar (8 untuk orde pertama, 14 untuk orde kedua) dan jumlah gate minimal (seperti di bagian sebelumnya). Qiskit tidak menemukan\n"
"pengelompokan itu sendiri. Kalau suku-sukunya didaftar ikatan demi ikatan (persegi), jumlah gate-nya sama, tetapi layer-nya tidak dipadatkan\n"
"dan kedalaman bertambah seiring lattice (pada $10\\times12$ menjadi 84 lawan 8 untuk orde pertama dan 166 lawan 14 untuk orde kedua).\n"
"Dengan `preserve_order=False` (segitiga), Qiskit memang menemukan suku-suku yang komut dan kedalamannya tetap datar, tetapi suku XX dan YY\n"
"dari satu ikatan diperlakukan sebagai rotasi terpisah, jadi butuh sekitar sepertiga lebih banyak gate dua-qubit dan dua kali kedalaman. Jadi level bosonik\n"
"bukan sulap: ia membawa pewarnaan sisi di dalam operator itu sendiri, dan apa yang kalau tidak harus kamu atur manual di suku\n"
"Pauli (dan dijaga tetap teratur untuk setiap lattice) sudah ikut dalam konstruksinya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "6. Transpile for Nighthawk {#6-transpile-for-nighthawk}"
msgstr "6. Transpile untuk Nighthawk {#6-transpile-for-nighthawk}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`FakeNighthawk` is a $12\\times10$ square lattice with qubit index $10\\,\\text{row} + \\text{col}$. A hard-core lattice is a square\n"
"lattice too, so it sits on the chip as it is: site $(x, y)$ goes to qubit $10y + x$, which embeds an $L_x\\times L_y$ lattice\n"
"natively for $L_x \\le 10$, $L_y \\le 12$ as shown below.\n"
msgstr ""
"`FakeNighthawk` adalah lattice persegi $12\\times10$ dengan indeks qubit $10\\,\\text{row} + \\text{col}$. Lattice hard-core juga lattice\n"
"persegi, jadi bisa langsung diletakkan di chip apa adanya: situs $(x, y)$ menuju qubit $10y + x$, yang menanamkan lattice $L_x\\times L_y$\n"
"secara native untuk $L_x \\le 10$, $L_y \\le 12$ seperti ditunjukkan di bawah.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/hard-core-bosons-dynamics/extracted-outputs/3508477b-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/hard-core-bosons-dynamics/extracted-outputs/3508477b-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, check the native embedding on the **unrouted** circuits. After lowering on the abstract register, every two-qubit gate must sit on a coupled pair under the layout.\n"
msgstr "Pertama, periksa penanaman native pada circuit yang **belum di-route**. Setelah diturunkan pada register abstrak, setiap gate dua-qubit harus berada pada pasangan yang terhubung menurut layout.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now route onto the chip. Every two-qubit gate is already on a coupler, so the transpiler has no swaps to insert and nothing to\n"
"choose: the routed circuit has the same two-qubit depth and the same two-qubit gate count as the circuit on the abstract\n"
"register, at every size. The cell below transpiles each lattice of the scaling study onto Nighthawk and asserts exactly that.\n"
"The drawing shows the routed circuit for the $4\\times4$ lattice. Each wire is labeled `q_i ↦ p`: virtual qubit `i` of the\n"
"encoded circuit (the lattice site `i`) sits on physical qubit `p` of the device at the start. Only the qubits the circuit acts\n"
"on are drawn.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang route ke chip. Setiap gate dua-qubit sudah berada di coupler, jadi transpiler tidak perlu menyisipkan swap dan tidak ada\n"
"yang perlu dipilih: circuit hasil routing punya kedalaman dua-qubit dan jumlah gate dua-qubit yang sama seperti circuit pada register\n"
"abstrak, di setiap ukuran. Sel di bawah men-transpile setiap lattice dari studi skala ke Nighthawk dan meng-assert hal itu.\n"
"Gambar menunjukkan circuit hasil routing untuk lattice $4\\times4$. Setiap kabel diberi label `q_i ↦ p`: qubit virtual `i` dari\n"
"circuit yang di-encode (situs lattice `i`) berada di qubit fisik `p` pada device di awal. Hanya qubit yang dipakai circuit\n"
"yang digambar.\n"

