# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "7. Beyond hard-core bosons: higher mode truncation {#7-beyond-hard-core-bosons-higher-mode-truncation}"
msgstr "7. Melampaui boson hard-core: truncation mode yang lebih tinggi {#7-beyond-hard-core-bosons-higher-mode-truncation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Everything so far only considered hard-core bosons, so the on-site term could not act. With $d = 3$, a site can\n"
"hold two bosons, $\\tfrac U2 n(n-1)$ appears as a third group (diagonal), and the hopping matrix elements acquire $\\sqrt2$ factors.\n"
"The next cell builds the Bose-Hubbard step on a 4-site chain and measures its cost the same way, for all four encodings, next to the hard-core chain of the same length.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sejauh ini semuanya hanya membahas boson hard-core, jadi suku on-site tidak bisa bekerja. Dengan $d = 3$, satu situs bisa\n"
"menampung dua boson, $\\tfrac U2 n(n-1)$ muncul sebagai grup ketiga (diagonal), dan elemen matriks hopping\n"
"mendapat faktor $\\sqrt2$.\n"
"Sel berikutnya membangun langkah Bose-Hubbard pada rantai 4 situs dan mengukur biayanya dengan cara yang sama, untuk keempat encoding, berdampingan dengan rantai hard-core dengan panjang yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The physics becomes significantly more complicated and the favorable scaling disappears.\n"
msgstr "Fisikanya menjadi jauh lebih rumit dan skala yang menguntungkan itu hilang.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial used hard-core bosons because they make for simple analyses while emphasizing the benefits of the `qiskit-bosons` package and architecture of its transpiler framework. It is set up to investigate real bosonic physics beyond such simple truncation limits, but exploring these circuits and researching their application is now up to you.\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini memakai boson hard-core karena memudahkan analisis sambil menonjolkan manfaat paket `qiskit-bosons` dan arsitektur kerangka transpiler-nya. Paket ini disiapkan untuk menyelidiki fisika bosonik yang nyata melampaui batas truncation sederhana seperti itu, tetapi menjelajahi circuit-circuit ini dan meneliti penerapannya sekarang terserah kamu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "8. Takeaways and next steps {#8-takeaways-and-next-steps}"
msgstr "8. Takeaway dan langkah selanjutnya {#8-takeaways-and-next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The output below recaps the circuit cost of a single Trotter step for the hard-core lattices, and the Trotter error of the small system.\n"
msgstr "Output di bawah merangkum biaya circuit dari satu langkah Trotter untuk lattice hard-core, dan error Trotter dari sistem kecil.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"From these numbers, you can draw some high-level takeaways. The first ones are about the framework, which is what you\n"
"carry over to other bosonic models. The later ones are about what the results show for hard-core bosons, the simple test case.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dari angka-angka ini, kamu bisa menarik beberapa takeaway tingkat tinggi. Yang pertama tentang kerangkanya, yang bisa\n"
"kamu bawa ke model bosonik lain. Yang berikutnya tentang apa yang ditunjukkan hasilnya untuk boson hard-core, kasus uji sederhana.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**A framework for bosonic physics.** `qiskit-bosons` separates three things: the model (a `BosonOperator`, grouped here\n"
"by edge color), the circuit (one `Evolution` gate and a Trotter formula that splits it), and the lowering to qubits (the mode\n"
"truncation $d$ and the `LevelEncoding`, chosen when the transpiler preset runs). Changing one of them leaves the other two\n"
"untouched (sections 2 and 7).\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kerangka untuk fisika bosonik.** `qiskit-bosons` memisahkan tiga hal: model (sebuah `BosonOperator`, di sini dikelompokkan\n"
"menurut warna sisi), circuit (satu gate `Evolution` dan rumus Trotter yang memecahnya), dan penurunan ke qubit (truncation\n"
"mode $d$ dan `LevelEncoding`, dipilih saat preset transpiler dijalankan). Mengubah satu hal tidak memengaruhi dua hal lainnya\n"
"(bagian 2 dan 7).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Why Trotterize at the bosonic level.** The grouping lives in the operator, so the Trotter circuit comes out with a flat depth\n"
"without any ordering by hand. One `PauliEvolutionGate` over the same qubit operator has the same Trotter error order and\n"
"scaling, and with the terms sorted by color it is the identical circuit. In another order, the depth grows with the lattice\n"
"(84 against 8 for one first-order step at $10\\times12$) or the gate count is about a third higher (sections 4 and 5).\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kenapa Trotterize di level bosonik.** Pengelompokan ada di dalam operator, jadi circuit Trotter keluar dengan kedalaman datar\n"
"tanpa pengurutan manual. Satu `PauliEvolutionGate` atas operator qubit yang sama punya orde error Trotter dan\n"
"skala yang sama, dan dengan suku diurutkan menurut warna, circuit-nya identik. Pada urutan lain, kedalaman bertambah seiring lattice\n"
"(84 lawan 8 untuk satu langkah orde pertama pada $10\\times12$) atau jumlah gate sekitar sepertiga lebih tinggi (bagian 4 dan 5).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Accuracy.** The only numerical error is the Trotter error between the colors, and it falls with the number of steps as\n"
"expected for first and second order (section 4). The qubit side and the encoding add nothing.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Akurasi.** Satu-satunya error numerik adalah error Trotter antar warna, dan error itu turun seiring jumlah langkah seperti\n"
"diharapkan untuk orde pertama dan kedua (bagian 4). Sisi qubit dan encoding tidak menambah apa-apa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The encoding is a cost choice.** At $d = 2$, all four encodings give the same physics. The compact codes need half the\n"
"qubits and are about 20 times cheaper in depth and gates than the unary ones (section 5).\n"
msgstr ""
"**Encoding adalah pilihan biaya.** Pada $d = 2$, keempat encoding memberikan fisika yang sama. Kode kompak butuh setengah\n"
"jumlah qubit dan sekitar 20 kali lebih murah dalam kedalaman dan gate dibanding kode unary (bagian 5).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Hardware.** With the natural embedding of the lattice, every gate already sits on a Nighthawk coupler, so the chip runs the\n"
"circuit with no routing overhead at any size up to the whole chip (section 6).\n"
msgstr ""
"**Hardware.** Dengan penanaman lattice yang natural, setiap gate sudah berada di coupler Nighthawk, jadi chip menjalankan\n"
"circuit tanpa overhead routing pada ukuran berapa pun sampai seluruh chip (bagian 6).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"* **Hard-core bosons are the entry point, not the goal.** They are the $U\\to\\infty$ limit of Bose-Hubbard, with the XY model as\n"
"  a spin-1/2 equivalent. They are exactly free fermions on an open chain but not on a square lattice, which makes 2D the\n"
"  interesting case (section 1). Raising the truncation to $d = 3$ brings the on-site interaction back and the cost jumps (a\n"
"  4-site chain goes from a two-qubit depth of 4 to 95 in the Gray code, section 7). That is where the exploration of bosonic\n"
"  physics begins, and the same framework carries it.\n"
"**Caveats.** All depths are for a noise-free fake backend (`FakeNighthawk`) and one fixed basis (`cz, rz, sx, x`, optimization\n"
"level 3); they compare structure, not fidelity. The routed numbers equal the abstract ones only because the natural embedding\n"
"puts every gate on a coupler. The Néel quench is one initial state; the Trotter error depends on the state and on $T$. Nothing\n"
"here runs on real hardware.\n"
msgstr ""
"* **Boson hard-core adalah titik awal, bukan tujuan.** Mereka adalah limit $U\\to\\infty$ dari Bose-Hubbard, dengan model XY sebagai\n"
"  padanan spin-1/2. Mereka persis fermion bebas pada rantai terbuka tetapi tidak pada lattice persegi, yang membuat 2D\n"
"  menjadi kasus yang menarik (bagian 1). Menaikkan truncation ke $d = 3$ membawa kembali interaksi on-site dan biayanya melonjak (rantai\n"
"  4 situs naik dari kedalaman dua-qubit 4 menjadi 95 pada kode Gray, bagian 7). Di situlah eksplorasi fisika\n"
"  bosonik dimulai, dan kerangka yang sama mendukungnya.\n"
"**Catatan.** Semua kedalaman berlaku untuk backend palsu tanpa noise (`FakeNighthawk`) dan satu basis tetap (`cz, rz, sx, x`, tingkat optimisasi\n"
"3); angka-angka ini membandingkan struktur, bukan fidelitas. Angka hasil routing sama dengan yang abstrak hanya karena penanaman natural\n"
"meletakkan setiap gate di coupler. Quench Néel hanyalah satu state awal; error Trotter bergantung pada state dan pada $T$. Tidak ada\n"
"yang di sini dijalankan di hardware nyata.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Next steps.** Hard-core bosons are a simple, checkable model to learn the framework on. From here, the same building\n"
"blocks apply to the models that are hard to treat classically:\n"
msgstr ""
"**Langkah selanjutnya.** Boson hard-core adalah model sederhana yang bisa dicek untuk mempelajari kerangka ini. Dari sini, blok bangunan\n"
"yang sama berlaku untuk model yang sulit ditangani secara klasik:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Larger cutoffs $d$ (soft-core bosons, the full Bose-Hubbard model), where the choice of encoding and of Trotter formula\n"
"matters much more than here (section 7)\n"
msgstr ""
"Cutoff $d$ yang lebih besar (boson soft-core, model Bose-Hubbard penuh), di mana pilihan encoding dan rumus Trotter\n"
"jauh lebih penting daripada di sini (bagian 7)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Other Hamiltonians, such as bosons with a different interaction or a different coupling to their environment\n"
msgstr "Hamiltonian lain, seperti boson dengan interaksi yang berbeda atau kopling yang berbeda ke lingkungannya\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Other lattices, such as triangular or honeycomb, which need other edge colorings and other hardware embeddings\n"
msgstr "Lattice lain, seperti segitiga atau honeycomb, yang butuh pewarnaan sisi lain dan penanaman hardware lain\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Correlation functions as observables, such as $\\langle X_iX_j + Y_iY_j\\rangle$ and density-density correlators\n"
msgstr "Fungsi korelasi sebagai observabel, seperti $\\langle X_iX_j + Y_iY_j\\rangle$ dan korelator densitas-densitas\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mixed models (bosons coupled to fermions or to a bath)\n"
msgstr "Model campuran (boson yang terkopel dengan fermion atau dengan bath)\n"

